speechtext:
What about, hospitals?
Mr. MaeNICOL: In some cases it is impossible to get them past the compensation boards because they have made their decision;
they have taken their stand against the man and are determined not to let him get compensation. Once the compensation board have given their decision they think it is like the laws of the Medes and Persians; their decision cannot be changed. In New Brunswick they have the right to appeal to the judge. I would take a chance before a judge because he would not be interested except in giving justice. He would call all kinds of medical men to give evidence and advice. Once a compensation board have come to a decision that tuberculosis is not caused in a plant, they will not change their decision and that is why nothing has come to the minister's attention in that regard.
